Subject: [PATCH] CLI: show OpenSync pods onboarded through an adapter

Topology nodes carry the device's manufacturer, model and a kind derived
from the manufacturer ("opensync-pod" for "OpenSync..."; needs 0209). The
topology view draws such a pod with its own icon and names its model and
manufacturer on hover, escaped: the agent chose those strings. The dashboard
lists a pod's own vendor and model. Node names stay as they are (Agent-N,
Extender-N), since the lab's checks read them. The root is always the
controller: its own record takes the last M1 the controller processed
("Banana Pi - R4", or an adapter's), so it is never classified by it.

Its page hunks (src/rdkb-cli/static) moved to easymesh-medium's topology-ui,
which builds the page the controller image serves.
---
--- a/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
+++ b/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
@@ -3415,8 +3415,12 @@
 		deviceSignal, legacySignal := classifyDeviceBackhaulSignal(
 			backhaulMetrics, getTreeValue(backhaul, "STAAddress"),
 			getTreeValue(backhaul, "MACAddress"), backhaulMedia, observedAt.UTC())
+		vendor, model := "RDK-B", "EasyMesh node"
+		if manufacturer, deviceModel, kind := deviceIdentity(deviceNode, depth); kind == "opensync-pod" {
+			vendor, model = manufacturer, deviceModel
+		}
 		inventoryDevices = append(inventoryDevices, Device{
-			MAC: deviceID, Role: role, Vendor: "RDK-B", Model: "EasyMesh node",
